# Normalise to LF in the repository; a shell script keeps working on a Mac.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: they must arrive with CRLF endings.
# A .cmd file with Unix line endings fails in a way that looks like nothing at
# all — the window opens and closes again, with no error to read.
#
# They are stored with real CRLF bytes and marked -text so that git never
# converts them in either direction. `eol=crlf` alone would not be enough:
# it is applied on checkout, and `git archive` — which is how the delivery
# zip is built — ignores it entirely and would ship Unix endings.
# The last matching rule wins, so these two lines stay below the one above.
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text
